.TH SEPARAN 1 "2026-09-26" "Separan 1.0.0" "Separan User Commands"
.SH NAME
separan \- run, validate, inspect, and format Separan source files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B separan
.RI [ source.sep ]
.RI [ arguments ... ]
.br
.B separan --check
.I source.sep
.br
.B separan --tokens
.I source.sep
.br
.B separan --structure
.I source.sep
.br
.B separan --tag
.I source.sep semantic-tag
.br
.B separan --verify-tag-scope
.I before.sep after.sep semantic-tag
.br
.B separan --format
.I source.sep
.br
.B separan -help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B separan
is the native Separan 1.0 command-line runtime. It executes labeled
Separan logic, validates source structure, prints lexer tokens or structure
metadata, verifies semantic-tag scope changes, and formats structural
indentation.
.PP
Separan uses explicit block identities such as
.BR SEP:name / END_SEP:name
and reports diagnostics with stable E-codes and source positions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI source.sep
Run the source file. Arguments following the source path are passed to the
Separan program through the command-argument context.
.TP
.B --check source.sep
Validate syntax, declarations, imports, labels, and supported structure
without executing top-level statements or the main function.
.TP
.B --tokens source.sep
Lex the source file and print a JSON array containing token type, lexeme, line,
and column.
.TP
.B --structure source.sep
Inspect named structures and print the native structural JSON result.
.TP
.BI "--tag " source.sep " " semantic-tag
Inspect functions and structures carrying the semantic tag and print JSON.
.TP
.BI "--verify-tag-scope " before.sep " " after.sep " " semantic-tag
Compare the tagged scope in two source files. The command returns success when
the tagged scope and its boundary remain valid and unchanged.
.TP
.B --format source.sep
Validate and print the source with structural indentation. The input file is
not modified.
.TP
.B -help
Print this help and exit successfully.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The requested operation completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
The source, arguments, file operation, JSON operation, or requested
verification was invalid. Diagnostics are written to standard error when
applicable.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Diagnostics use the form
.PP
.EX
SEPARAN E104: message at line 3, column 7
.EE
.PP
Structured validation APIs additionally expose category, description, expected,
actual, primary position, and related opening-block position where applicable.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run a program:
.EX
separan examples/hello.sep
.EE
.TP
Check source in CI:
.EX
separan --check app.sep
.EE
.TP
Format without changing the file:
.EX
separan --format app.sep > app.formatted.sep
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/man/man1/separan.1
Installed manual page location on Unix-like systems.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR separan (1)
.PP
The native tree also provides the development gateway worker
.BR separan-gw,
which reads one HTTP request JSON object per stdin line and writes one response
JSON object per stdout line. It is the adapter boundary for future FastCGI and
socket transports.
.br
